      "side": 1,
      "message": "Jeremy, I want to chat about this tomorrow. We\u0027re seeing increased tests that are failing based on test order. Our initial goal was to have them in a single binary in order to optimize both runtime and compile time, but I worry it\u0027s coming at too high of a maintenance cost. Some initial thoughts:\n\n1. This CL will allow us to split the tests without having to also split the configs/dts. This should reduce some of the mental overhead of splitting up the tests.\n2. The tests that are split off are simple libraries, once we do fix the test order dependencies we can run the tests in a single binary again fairly easily.\n3. This is likely how we\u0027ll be adding project inheritence to twister eventually so it should also work well moving forward.\n\nI\u0027m putting a -1 verified on this right now because the `led_driver` test is failing. It seems there\u0027s a dependency on having an active charge port that\u0027s not satisfied when running alone. I hope Al might be able to resolve this since he wrote the test.",
