      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like the general idea here, and that it is so easy to split off a subdir.\n\nWouldn\u0027t it be simpler though to just add a BUILD.py to the subdir, since it doesn\u0027t depend on any of the source code in the parent dir?\n\nI think the steps are this:\n\n* Switch `zephyr_interface_library_named` to `project` to the subdir/CMakeLists.txt file.\n* Switch `zephyr_library_sources(` to `target_sources(app PRIVATE`\n* Add a BUILD.py to the subdir.\n* Remove add_subdirectory from the top level CMakeLists.txt\n\nYou could even leave the old code commented out with a TODO to fix the test order dependency.\n\nIf it\u0027s not as simple as I seem to think, then I\u0027m ok with this change as well.\n\nJack, do you have any ideas for a simple way to accomplish what Yuvall is trying to do?  He wants to split some srcs out into a new test, but only temporarily, so it should be really simple to split or unsplit those srcs.",
