      "side": 1,
      "message": "The projects do depend on some base set of sources. Basically we have the following as the \"core\" dependencies:\n\n```\n  src/main.c\n  src/test_mocks.c\n  src/test_rules.c\n  src/utils.c\n  src/stubs.c\n  include/\n  Kconfig\n  overlay.dts\n  prj.conf\n```\n\nThen each, sub-test can add overlays, `.conf` files, sources, and headers. So if the sub-directory turned into a project, you wouldn\u0027t be able to add the sources unless you did `../src/main.c` etc. That\u0027s possible, but it also means that every sub-test needs to keep track of the dependencies so if we ever add one or change one we\u0027ll have a cascading effect. It would be easier (mentally) to have the common logic as a library instead of a project, but I think that makes an even bigger change than what this CL and might not be worth it (yet)",
